 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The double denial",
   "texto": [
    "**Ne** goes in front of the conjugated verb and the negative word usually goes later: **Je ne travaille plus**, **Je ne fais rien**, **Je ne parle à personne**. In composite pass, **ne** goes before the auxiliary and **rien/personne** after: **Je n'ai rien mangé**, **Je n'ai vu personne**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "When «rien» or «personne» are the subject",
   "texto": [
    "You can also go before the verb: **Personne ne vient** (no one comes), **Rien ne va** (nothing goes well). The position depends on its function: as a subject they go before; as a complement they usually go after the verb or the auxiliary."
   ]
  },
